{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-06-working-across-background-subagents.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-23T16:34:52.069643Z","id":"25974834a9d84cf421502179b8d0c170645a16e329a608916e53cb58bb66bbd7","body":{"detail":"Line 19 (Review Focus 3) and line 27 (Task 1) say that replacing a record's threads without `background` drops the flag from threads no longer named and the lapse returns to 120 s. The code does the opposite (Working::set in crates/clax-core/src/working.rs keeps every background thread; test a_plain_call_replaces_only_the_foreground_threads), and line 28 of the same task says so. Lines 17 and 36 name a_turn_end_keeps_the_background_threads_and_ends_the_others and a_background_thread_outlives_a_publish_and_the_turn_and_ends_with_the_reply; the tests are a_turn_end_ends_the_foreground_work_and_carries_the_background_threads_on (working.rs) and a_background_thread_outlives_a_publish_and_a_plain_call_and_ends_with_the_reply (crates/clax-server/tests/api_working.rs). Line 30 counts eight background tests; the module has twelve.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"881d9ab7988162b9ad80a403d92bcb4c95f7978df8046ad5f848584186717830"},"suggested_fix":"Rewrite lines 19 and 27 to the shipped rule, correct the two test names and the count.","summary":"The plan still states the superseded rule that a plain working call drops unnamed background flags, and names tests that do not exist","tags":["review","review:pr-90-r2","session:claude-code:386e8a7b-06ac-481d-becf-93b54c67f51c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-06-working-across-background-subagents.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-23T16:37:40.043874Z","id":"b7f64c549d9b4626752b209f7a2b001ddee3b68508eda1d4c918e713288a4fcf","body":{"detail":"Checked at a6dd0dda7. Line 19: 'Re-naming a record's threads without `background` drops the flag from threads no longer named, and the lapse returns to 120 s.' Line 27: 'without it, replacing the threads keeps flags only on threads still named.' The code keeps them: `Working::set` in crates/clax-core/src/working.rs:549-553 retains every background thread in `r.threads` on a plain call and never touches `r.background`, and the test `a_plain_call_replaces_only_the_foreground_threads` (working.rs:1526-1545) asserts that after a plain call naming only t3 the record has thread_ids [t1, t3], background_thread_ids [t1] and expires_at now + BACKGROUND_TTL_SECS. Line 28 of the same task states the shipped rule ('a plain `set` replaces only foreground threads'), so the plan contradicts itself. Test names: `grep -rn 'a_turn_end_keeps_the_background_threads_and_ends_the_others\\|a_background_thread_outlives_a_publish_and_the_turn_and_ends_with_the_reply' --include='*.rs' --include='*.md' --include='*.ts' .` matches only lines 17 and 36 of this plan. The tests are `a_turn_end_ends_the_foreground_work_and_carries_the_background_threads_on` (crates/clax-core/src/working.rs:1366) and `a_background_thread_outlives_a_publish_and_a_plain_call_and_ends_with_the_reply` (crates/clax-server/tests/api_working.rs:428); line 36's other name, `background_names_the_threads_it_applies_to`, exists (api_working.rs:518). Count: line 30 says 'the eight background tests at the end of the module's tests'; `awk 'NR>=1333' crates/clax-core/src/working.rs | grep -c '#\\[test\\]'` prints 12 (working.rs:1355-1595, from `background_threads_join_the_record_without_replacing_its_threads` to `background_threads_are_served_only_when_there_are_some`), and `git diff main...HEAD -- crates/clax-core/src/working.rs` adds exactly those twelve test functions. Kind suggestion is right: a documentation correction, no behaviour involved.","kind":"comment","references":"25974834a9d84cf421502179b8d0c170645a16e329a608916e53cb58bb66bbd7","summary":"confirmed: lines 19 and 27 state the superseded rule, lines 17 and 36 name two tests that do not exist, and line 30 counts eight background tests where there are twelve","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:386e8a7b-06ac-481d-becf-93b54c67f51c"]}}
